    "background_story": "Shorty was a Little Bittern (Ixobrychus minutus), a small but fierce bird of the wetlands. He lived in a dense marsh, where his mottled brown plumage allowed him to blend seamlessly into the surroundings. Shorty was a master of stealth, using his camouflage to sneak up on unsuspecting fish and frogs. Despite his small size, he was a formidable hunter, with a sharp beak and lightning-fast reflexes. Shorty's home was a labyrinth of reeds and waterways, where he would often stand motionless, waiting for prey to wander into his strike zone. His patience and cunning earned him the respect of his fellow marsh dwellers, who admired his ability to thrive in the harsh but beautiful environment of the wetlands.",
